The generated handler uses `mscratch` as the GPR save-area pointer and restores all GPRs before `mret`; a true re-entrant save/restore would need a separate nested frame protocol and careful interaction with riscv-dv’s generated register choices. I’m going to implement the explicit documented waiver path for matched nested traps, with evidence recorded, because that is the safer harness fix here and does not relax mismatches before the nesting point.
