codex
The root of seed 2026061852 is a generated-handler bug: the handler uses `t1` as the restore-frame base and then restores `t1` from `24(t1)` before it has finished the remaining loads. Spike then faults on the next load using the clobbered base; the DUT’s simple memory model does not fault the same way, so streams split. This is still harness/handler design, not RTL evidence from the random program body.
