codex
The practical harness hardening is to stop using riscv-dv’s generated GPR restore block for the injected sync-trap resume path. That block can self-clobber its base register; I’m changing the adapter so the injected handler advances `mepc` and `mret`s directly, avoiding potentially faulting restore loads. This keeps DUT and Spike executing the same architectural stream and removes the unsafe handler dependency.
apply patch
